19:T44c,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the DAAD admission database guarantee admission?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It provides orientation. The selected German higher education institution makes the final decision for the exact programme."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a VPD?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A VPD is a preliminary review document issued by uni-assist for certain universities. You normally submit it in a separate direct university application before the deadline."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a VPD take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"uni-assist states that VPD processing usually takes four to six weeks after the complete online application is submitted."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do all international applicants need Studienkolleg?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It depends on the school qualification, prior study, intended subject and the institution's decision. Check the admission database and programme instructions."}}]}1:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","className":"editorial-page editorial-page--guide","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://aspirecompass.org/guides/study-in-germany-admission-requirements/\",\"name\":\"Study in Germany: admission requirements for international students\",\"description\":\"Check Germany admission requirements by degree and qualification. Compare direct, uni-assist and VPD routes, language evidence and document preparation.\",\"url\":\"https://aspirecompass.org/guides/study-in-germany-admission-requirements/\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-10-08\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-10-21\",\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://aspirecompass.org/images/programme-research-editorial.webp\",\"